+3. **Poor masks and obscured mark — NOT ADDRESSED (partially improved).** `components/arrival-hero.module.css:7` substitutes a coarse polygon for the original rectangular center. It retains a conspicuous, angular black background halo above the helmet and outside both shoulders/arms. The straight polygon edges remain clearly visible against the silver mark and purple background. The Z/sword is now readable, but the K remains mostly hidden by this unnecessary retained background. The right secondary photo still has a hard top edge. Additionally, sizing the whole original source box with aspect-ratio and then clipping to its interior shrinks the actual visible central athlete into a floating waist-up figure: near-final 1536×1024 image shows visible helmet around y175 and fading torso by y550, leaving a large empty lower-middle area. At 390×844 the central image fades out around y360 while identity starts around y490. At 320×568 the athlete's visible body is only roughly y110–250 and no longer the dominant visual. This is not a demand for unavailable full-body detail: enlarge/reposition the existing authentic torso to preserve prominence and use a close, softly feathered silhouette or an alternative clean source-preserving blend. Evidence: `/tmp/hero-r1-desktop-motion-end.png`, `/tmp/hero-r1-desktop-static.png`, `/tmp/hero-r1-mobile-static.png`, `/tmp/hero-r1-small-static.png`.
+
+4. **Static/no-JS viewport fit — NOT ADDRESSED across required short screens (portrait cases fixed).** Desktop 1536×1024 and portrait 390×844 / 320×568 now fit headline/footer within the viewport; 320×568 no-JS was separately captured and inspected. However, `components/arrival-hero.module.css:13` does not fit the content at 844×390 landscape. Measured hero y64–374: headline y237.89–367.23; school y377.23–391.23; WATCH THE FILM y401.23–434.23. The school and watch button are clipped entirely by hero overflow, and footer y350.70–364.70 overlaps REMEMBER. Natural scrolling cannot reveal these children because the section clips them. Use a dedicated short-landscape layout or content-aware sizing that keeps the actual copy/actions usable. Evidence: `/tmp/hero-r1-landscape.png`.
+
+5. **Initial sequence starts with visible collage / inconsistent lines — ADDRESSED.** `components/use-arrival-hero-motion.ts:20–25` initializes all reveal targets explicitly. Initial desktop has both headline lines at opacity 0, front athlete at 0, mark at 0, and visible dark rear #17. The captured near-final frame has athlete/headline opacity 1. Dynamic reduced motion after a near-final desktop scroll removes pin and restores opacity 1 / transform none. The newly hidden interactive details cause the distinct regression below.
+
+6. **Insufficient regressions — ADDRESSED for the original scoped repair requirements, with remaining limitations.** `tests/e2e/arrival-campaign.spec.ts:36–108` now includes active-pin-to-reduced cleanup, mobile and no-JS bounds, touch tablet exclusion, explicit initial-line state, and a photo-free component fixture. These meaningfully improve the prior two tests. The fixture confirms an empty-photo component makes no crop requests; it does not independently prove app-level preview configuration, which remains a source-reviewed/controller validation item. Tests still need the landscape and invisible keyboard-focus regressions below. Bounds/alt text cannot verify silhouette quality or dominance; screenshot review remains necessary. I did not run these tests; controller owns their post-build result.
+
+## New Important regression
+
+7. **Keyboard focus moves onto invisible hero controls at initial desktop state.** `components/use-arrival-hero-motion.ts:23` sets all `[data-arrival-detail]` to opacity 0, including the focusable watch button and scroll link (`components/arrival-hero.tsx:41,44`), with no focus reveal or temporary interaction handling. Using ordinary Tab keys from page load at 1536×1024, Tab step 11 focused WATCH THE FILM and step 12 focused SCROLL TO EXPLORE; both had computed opacity `0`, and scrollY remained 0. A keyboard user loses the focus indicator and can activate unseen actions. Preserve visible keyboard focus and operable navigation throughout the reveal, for example by revealing controls/the final frame on keyboard focus, or otherwise ensuring focus never lands on an invisible control. Add a real Tab-navigation assertion.
+
+## Measurements, preservation, and limits
+
+Ran standalone Chromium captures/DOM measurements only: `/tmp/hero-task-r1-review.cjs`, `/tmp/hero-r1-extra.cjs`, plus an inline landscape/Tab probe. Outputs are `/tmp/hero-r1-*.png`, outside test-results. Sizes inspected: 1536×1024 static/reduced/no-JS/initial/near-final/dynamic-reduce; 390×844 static and default motion; 320×568 reduced/no-JS; 768×1024 static; 1024×768 touch; 1280×600 short desktop; 844×390 touch landscape. No horizontal document overflow measured in the repeated portrait/static probes. Face/#17 remain authentic and visible, although central subject prominence regressed as described above.
+
